Chunk 12 mentions naming rules for user IDs. It says the user ID can't be certain names like USERS, ADMINS, etc., and can't start with IBM, SQL, SYS. The example names are JoeSmith and joesmith, showing case sensitivity. The instance owner name must match an existing user ID exactly. 

