Also, on RHEL (which is Linux), the primary group of the instance owner must be valid. The user would need to create the user with the correct primary group, possibly using the idsadduser command as shown in chunk 16. 

Additionally, the instance owner must be a member of the idsldap group, as per chunk 8 and 17. So when creating the user, they need to assign the primary group and ensure the user is in the required groups. 

